From c2fcd4476ee8878846a985b7163fcc3eaea0c0b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:00:40 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Indy (mips64 n32): bootstrap entry, Seeq 8003 driver,
 big-endian fixes

- bootstrap/src/mips64.rs, mips64.ld: the bootstrap's entry and layout for
  elf32-ntradbigmips; USERMODE_END is 0x8000_0000.
- bootstrap/src/initnsmgr.rs: decode numbers in native byte order, as
  redox-rt encodes them (a big-endian machine read dup kind 2 as 0x02000000).
- drivers/net/seeqd: Seeq 8003 behind the HPC3 DMA engines, fixed physical
  addresses, MAC from the DS1386 NVRAM, a 16-descriptor receive ring and one
  transmit descriptor, polled on a 10 ms timer.
- drivers/common/src/dma.rs: DMA memory is uncached on mips64.
- netstack: read /etc/net/<key> from the initfs when there is no root
  filesystem.
- Cargo.toml: redox_syscall and libc from the fork's vendored copies;
  bootstrap takes redox-rt from the local relibc checkout.

Signed-off-by: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
